<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bellum Iugurthinum</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 40 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a> · Also known as The Jugurthine War</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Bellum Iugurthinum is a historical monograph by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sallust">Sallust</a>, written around 40 BCE, on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>'s war against the Numidian king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jugurtha">Jugurtha</a> in 112–105 BCE. Using the war to show the corruption of the Roman nobility and the rise of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaius-marius">Gaius Marius</a>, it also includes a description of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-africa">North Africa</a> and its peoples drawn partly from Punic books. It is a principal source for Numidian history.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bellum-iugurthinum.jpg" alt="Bellum Iugurthinum" width="320" height="144" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CNG · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sulla_Coin2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
